
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">People say that philosophers have been working on the same questions for thousands of years. True, we are persistent&#8212;thanks for noticing! But it&#8217;s also the case that philosophers are often working on <em>new </em>questions, ones that did not exist thousands or hundreds of years ago, or even decades ago. We&#8217;re inventive, too!</p>



<span id="more-27597"></span>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Today is <a href="https://www.unesco.org/en/days/philosophy">World Philosophy Day</a>. To mark the occasion, I thought it would be a good idea to let people know what philosophers are asking about <em>today</em>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For that, I&#8217;ll need your help. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Philosophers, please take a moment to write down, in a comment on this post, one question you are currently working on.</strong> (Yes,<em> just <strong>one</strong>.</em>)</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="589" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/exclamation-to-question-2-1024x589.png" alt="" class="wp-image-27599" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/exclamation-to-question-2-1024x589.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/exclamation-to-question-2-300x173.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/exclamation-to-question-2-768x442.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/exclamation-to-question-2-1536x883.png 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/exclamation-to-question-2-2048x1178.png 2048w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/exclamation-to-question-2-250x144.png 250w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It would also help if you shared the post and encouraged other philosophers to comment with a question they’re working on. The result could be a picture of what philosophers are thinking about today, parts of which perhaps catch the attention of people who otherwise might have not realized they are interested in what philosophers are up to.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thank you!</p>



